The packet distinguishes three ways an arm can be dead: its pattern is impossible, its guard is contradictory, or earlier arms cover it. I’ll track those separately.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- Exhaustiveness depends on coverage the checker can prove. An opaque guard can match at runtime but contributes no certain coverage.
- Each arm needs its own scope. That lets the checker detect both rebinding an outer name and using a neighbour’s binding.
